    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="s8"><span class="secnum">8</span>Limits, and what was tried</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>It measures nothing.</strong> The report reads the files the blocks wrote. A figure that was not
      measured is not listed, and a section of a block that has not run says so.</li>
      <li><strong>Details the files do not give stay empty until typed.</strong> Instrument, mount, filter, location
      and date are never guessed. The pasted text holds only what is known.</li>
      <li><strong>The spectral response is approximate.</strong> Star spectra are broad and alike, so different curves
      explain the same stars about equally well. On synthetic stars the shapes come back close to the true ones, but
      the response at the Hα line came out 0.76 for a true 0.59, about 30 % off. No error band is drawn: neither
      resampling the stars nor varying the smoothing measured that error.</li>
      <li><strong>Sizes in pixels without a scale.</strong> If the scale on the sky is not known, the star size is
      given in pixels, and the figures say so.</li>
      <li><strong>Outdated results.</strong> After a change to the workflow, the report shows the results the blocks
      had at their last run until the workflow is run again.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

